From: TB378FC Maintainers <tb378fc@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] va, codec: support Chromium VaapiVideoEncodeAccelerator sticky CBR & hint buffers

1. Accept and harmlessly ignore optional VA-API encode hint/packed/QP/matrix
   buffers in createBuffer() and renderPicture() so clients never fail with
   VA_STATUS_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_BUFFERTYPE.
2. Persist VAEncMiscParameterRateControl and VAEncMiscParameterFrameRate
   across subsequent P-frames in H264Encoder and HevcEncoder (Chromium sets
   sequence.bits_per_second = 0 and only submits RateControl on IDR or rate
   changes, which previously failed "CBR needs a bitrate" on Frame 1).
3. Honour VBR target_percentage (1..99) in VAEncMiscParameterRateControl.

